# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .env.production is the one exception to the blanket .env.* ignore above: it carries the public
# deployment's build-time config (8-02), and none of its three values are secrets (see the file's
# own header comment) - Vite's own convention treats a committed .env.production as normal, only
# .env.local/.env.*.local (real per-developer overrides) are meant to stay uncommitted.
!.env.production
# `15-11`: `.env.ux-gate` is the identical shape of exception, for the identical reason - see its own
# header comment. Localhost placeholders, not secrets.
!.env.ux-gate

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# `15-11`: the rendered UX gate (`ux-gate/`) is source; everything it *produces* is a build artifact -
# screenshots, Playwright's own HTML report and trace/output directories. CI publishes the
# screenshots via `actions/upload-artifact` rather than a commit (`ci.yml`'s own "Rendered UX gate"
# step), the same "the commit determines the artifact" reasoning `ci.yml`'s existing comment on the
# image build already states for the console's own Docker image.
/ux-gate/screenshots/
/ux-gate/test-results/
/ux-gate/playwright-report/
/ux-gate/blob-report/
